@* The only sanctioned horizontal scroll in the app (ADR 0003).

   WCAG 2.1 SC 1.4.10 exempts "parts of the content which require
   two-dimensional layout for usage or meaning". Five components claim that
   exception — source viewer, explorer two-pane grid, wide data tables, the
   policy category grid, and the DAST request/response panels — and each
   scrolls INSIDE ITSELF rather than pushing the page.

   The page body must never scroll horizontally at 320px. If you are reaching
   for this outside those five, the layout needs a breakpoint instead. *@

<div class="scroll-x @Class" role="region" aria-label="@Label" tabindex="0">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
    /// <summary>Named so a screen reader can announce the scrollable region.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
